Subject: [PATCH sched_ext/for-7.5 0/2] selftests/sched_ext: Catch schedulers that fail to enable
To: Tejun Heo <tj@kernel.org>
Cc: David Vernet <void@manifault.com>,
    Andrea Righi <arighi@nvidia.com>,
    Changwoo Min <changwoo@igalia.com>,
    Tao Cui <cuitao@kylinos.cn>,
    Ching-Chun Huang <jserv@ccns.ncku.edu.tw>,
    Chia-Ping Tsai <chia7712@gmail.com>,
    sched-ext@lists.linux.dev,
    linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org

When a root scheduler fails late in scx_root_enable_workfn(), the
kernel records the error for ops.exit() and still completes the attach
successfully. A test that only checks the attach therefore passes even
though the scheduler never ran. With cache detection failing for CPU 0,
scx_root_enable() fails with -22 for every scheduler, yet minimal and
select_cpu_dfl report ok. select_cpu_dispatch and total_bw only check
results that a scheduler which never ran also produces.

  1: add SCX_ASSERT_ENABLED(), which checks /sys/kernel/sched_ext/state,
     and share the state read with the runner's leftover-scheduler check
  2: use it in those four tests

This series is on top of "selftests/sched_ext: Fix scheduler leaks on
early return", which adds the test context helpers and the runner check
it uses.

Tested with vng on for-7.5 plus that series: all tests pass, with
enq_blocked and nohz_tick skipped as they need CONFIG_SCHED_PROXY_EXEC
and nohz_full=. With cache detection forced to fail for CPU 0, the four
tests now fail with "Scheduler is not enabled (state: disabled)".

checkpatch --strict is clean on both patches.

Cheng-Yang Chou (2):
  selftests/sched_ext: Add SCX_ASSERT_ENABLED() to catch failed enables
  selftests/sched_ext: Check that the scheduler gets enabled in four
    tests

